# Environment variables read by the code. All are optional: the defaults work for tiers 0 and 1
# (docs/reproduction.md). The code reads the process environment: uncomment and edit what you need, then load
# the file into your shell with
#   cp .env.example .env   # edit, then:   set -a; source .env; set +a
# Never commit real keys or personal paths: .env is gitignored.

# ── Analysis tier and data ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Data root read by paper/: the directory that contains results/ (the unpacked results archive).
# Default: <repo_root>/data
# FLIPS_DATA=/path/to/unpacked/archive

# Output root of paper/make_paper.py. Default: <repo_root>/paper/out
# FLIPS_OUT=/path/to/output

# Source of scripts/fetch_data.py: a Zenodo record URL (.../records/<id>) or a direct archive URL.
# FLIPS_DATA_URL=https://zenodo.org/records/<id>

# Number of numba threads for the feature statistics (tier 2). Default: 4
# FLIPS_NUM_THREADS=8

# ── Generation (tier 4) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Directory holding the model weights, one folder per model: $AUDIT_LLM_MODEL_CACHE/<org>/<model>
# (scripts/Run_Inferences.py loads the weights and tokenizers from there). When unset, the Hugging Face hub ids
# are resolved through the Hugging Face cache (download a model's repository once, e.g. with `huggingface-cli download <id>`, before the first run).
# AUDIT_LLM_MODEL_CACHE=/path/to/models

# Hugging Face cache root, used when downloading weights and tokenizers. Default: ~/.cache/huggingface
# HF_HOME=/path/to/hf/cache

# On a machine without network access: use the weights and tokenizers of the Hugging Face cache only.
# HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
